{"title":"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What number should be placed in the box to make <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/e/03e068ca927df5d5a5455fba3510c80066405a07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{4} \\times 100^{\\Box} = 1000^{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"155\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/5/335ed2bbef9fac7ea94fbbdf6e84e02a5fce8014.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 7 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 5 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 2 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ \\text{3}{2} \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"405\" height=\"18\" />  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the number represented by the box. To make the values easier to compute, we can make the exponents the same.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/4/924ebacfc60ef00a243c1ea0e6f601b27bea3b65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{4} \\times 100^{x} = 1000^{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"153\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/b/85b00315cac3eca45272161fb6faab3ece3eaef2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{4} \\times (10^{2})^{x} = (10^{3})^{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"169\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/9/a390695c485710bccba6096fad280d53f2032a1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{4} \\times 10^{2x} = 10^{18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/3/423ef06828ff69a19b5855780f4d1c3249789468.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{2x + 4} = 10^{18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Equating the exponents, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/8/91814200b90b0aad43c08bf38b2b9c2ee30fa20a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x + 4 = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/3/1f36c2c286cfe602597752ef16ee8fb933dddcf9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/c/b7c065ee540457f71aea1fbc7ecaceb5e0da4dad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\boxed {\\textbf {(A) } 7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"92\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Prob